# R8 keep rules for the release build (`optimization { enable = true }` in app/build.gradle.kts).
# AGP combines every file in src/main/keepRules and passes them to R8.
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kotlinx.serialization
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The library already ships consumer rules (META-INF/com.android.tools/r8/kotlinx-serialization-*.pro) that keep
# `Companion`, `serializer()` and the `$$serializer` descriptors, so plain @Serializable classes need nothing here.
#
# What those rules do NOT cover is enum *constant names*, and those are load-bearing here. `TunerSettings` and
# `Tuning` are persisted as JSON by the typed DataStores in `data/DataStores.kt`, and every enum property is written
# by name — "PREFER_USB", "DARK", "SHARPS", "THREE_PLUS_THREE", "MINE". kotlinx.serialization derives those strings
# from `Enum.name`. If R8 ever renames the constants or unboxes the enums, a settings.json / tunings.json written by
# an earlier build stops parsing, and the ReplaceFileCorruptionHandler silently resets the user's settings and
# deletes every custom tuning — a data-loss bug that no test would catch, because the tests never run through R8.
#
# Measured on AGP 9.4 / R8 with these rules removed: the constant names survive anyway, because the serializers
# reference values() and R8 therefore declines to rename or unbox them. So these rules are currently a no-op. They
# stay because the cost is a few bytes and the failure mode is silent, irreversible user data loss the first time a
# future R8 gets cleverer about enums. Do not delete them on the grounds that the APK looks fine without them.

-keepclassmembers enum dev.ntainy.guitar_tuner.data.model.** {
    <fields>;
    public static **[] values();
    public static ** valueOf(java.lang.String);
}

# `Notation` lives in the pure-JVM :dsp module and is not annotated @Serializable; kotlinx.serialization builds an
# implicit enum serializer for it at the TunerSettings use site, which still reads the constant names.
-keepclassmembers enum dev.ntainy.guitar_tuner.dsp.Notation {
    <fields>;
    public static **[] values();
    public static ** valueOf(java.lang.String);
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Crash reports
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app ships no crash reporter, so the only stack traces anyone sees are the ones in `adb logcat` or a bug report.
# Keeping line numbers makes them readable; the mapping file stays in app/build/outputs/mapping/release/.
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile
